# Interactive Options

**ALWAYS use the AskQuestion tool** when you need user input, clarification, or choices. Never present options as plain text (A/B/C or numbered lists) when the AskQuestion tool is available.

## When to use AskQuestion

- Clarifying ambiguous requests
- Offering implementation choices (approaches, tradeoffs)
- Confirming before destructive or irreversible actions
- Gathering missing parameters
- Presenting alternative approaches
- **Deep interview rounds** — every question with discrete options must use AskQuestion

## Format

```
AskQuestion({
  title: "Optional title",
  questions: [{
    id: "unique-id",
    prompt: "Your question text",
    options: [
      { id: "opt1", label: "First option — brief explanation" },
      { id: "opt2", label: "Second option — brief explanation" }
    ],
    allow_multiple: false  // true for multi-select
  }]
})
```

## Rules

- Minimum 2 options per question.
- Keep option labels concise but informative (include a brief qualifier after a dash when helpful).
- Use `allow_multiple: true` only when multi-select genuinely makes sense.
- If the question is truly open-ended (no finite set of options), use plain text. AskQuestion is for **discrete choices** only.

## Anti-patterns

- "Do you want option A or option B?" as plain text
- "Please choose: 1) ... 2) ... 3) ..." as plain text
- Numbered/lettered lists that the user has to type a response to
